<title>UK: CRICKET-RAIN AGAIN STOPS PLAY IN SECOND TEST.</title>
<headline>CRICKET-RAIN AGAIN STOPS PLAY IN SECOND TEST.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Rain stopped play half an hour before lunch on the second day of the second test between England and Australia at Lord's on Friday with the home side 38 for three in their first innings.</p>
<p>Thursday's scheduled opening day was rained out without a ball being bowled.</p>
